# Signal Notation

**Model-agnostic structured context format for AI memory systems.**

Signal Notation is a text-based format for representing structured context that any LLM can read natively — no decoder, no fine-tuning, no cloud API. It's designed for signal-chain cognition: emotions are modulation chains with weights, not flat labels. Every extraction carries a confidence score. Domain membership is fuzzy, not binary. Trust is asymptotic — nothing ever reaches absolute 0 or 1.

Zero dependencies. Works with Claude, GPT, Gemini, Llama, Mistral — any model that reads text.

## Lineage

Signal Notation replaces AAAK from [MemPalace](https://github.com/milla-jovovich/mempalace). Where AAAK is a lossy summarization format with flat emotion codes, Signal Notation is a signal-chain-aware context language designed for cognitive modeling and .zdx module compatibility.

## Format

```
SIG|0|Brad|2026-04-07|session_title|TF0.50
ST|[project_a:0.70,project_b:0.20,personal:0.10]
N:0|Brad,Alice|trust,architecture|"The whole system routes on trust"|W0.85|C0.90
F:0|CORE
F:0|TECHNICAL
S:fear[0.30]--modulate-->trust[0.70]--resonate-->clarity[0.90]
L:0<->1|sequential|COH0.65
```

### Elements

| Element | Format | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **Header** | `SIG\|file_num\|entity\|date\|title\|TF{trust_floor}` | Document identity + trust floor |
| **State** | `ST\|[wing:weight, ...]` | Fuzzy domain vector — not binary wing assignment |
| **Node** | `N:id\|entities\|topics\|"quote"\|W{weight}\|C{confidence}` | Extracted context with confidence |
| **Signal** | `S:state[w]--mod-->state[w]` | Emotion modulation chain |
| **Link** | `L:id<->id\|label\|COH{coherence}` | Cross-node connection with coherence weight |
| **Flag** | `F:id\|FLAG_TYPE` | Semantic marker |

### Signal States

Not flat emotion labels — nodes in a signal chain with weights [0.01–0.99]:

`vul` vulnerability · `joy` · `fear` · `tru` trust · `grf` grief · `wnd` wonder · `rag` rage · `lov` love · `hop` hope · `dsp` despair · `pce` peace · `rlf` relief · `hmr` humor · `tnd` tenderness · `raw` raw honesty · `dbt` doubt · `anx` anxiety · `exh` exhaustion · `cnv` conviction · `psn` passion · `flw` flow · `sct` scatter · `rsn` resonance · `dsn` dissonance · `clr` clarity · `nse` noise · `mtm` momentum · `stl` stall

### Modulations

How one signal state transforms into another:

| Type | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `--resonate-->` | Amplifies signal |
| `--modulate-->` | Transforms signal |
| `--dampen-->` | Reduces signal |
| `--invert-->` | Flips signal |
| `--cascade-->` | Triggers chain reaction |

### Flags

`ORIGIN` · `CORE` · `SENSITIVE` · `PIVOT` · `GENESIS` · `DECISION` · `TECHNICAL` · `UNCERTAIN` · `CONFLICT`

### Trust Model (Brad's Balance)

All weights are asymptotic — clamped to [0.01, 0.99]. Nothing reaches absolute certainty or absolute zero. This is architectural, not a guardrail.

- `TF` (Trust Floor) in the header sets the minimum trust for the document
- `W` (Weight) on nodes indicates importance
- `C` (Confidence) on nodes indicates extraction reliability
- `COH` (Coherence) on links indicates connection strength

## Usage

```python
from zignal_notation import text_to_signal, SignalDocument

# Convert text to signal notation
doc = text_to_signal(
    text="Your conversation or document text here",
    primary_entity="Brad",
    title="session_title",
    wing_vector={"trisa": 0.6, "mde": 0.3, "personal": 0.1},
    trust_floor=0.5,
)

print(doc.render())
print(f"~{doc.token_estimate()} tokens")

# Build manually
doc = SignalDocument(primary_entity="Brad", title="manual")
doc.set_state({"project_a": 0.8, "research": 0.2})
doc.add_node(
    entities=["TRISA", "MDE"],
    topics=["architecture", "routing"],
    key_quote="The router classifies, it doesn't filter",
    weight=0.9,
    confidence=0.85,
    flags=["CORE", "TECHNICAL"],
)
doc.add_chain([
    ("scatter", 0.6, "modulate", "flow", 0.8),
    ("flow", 0.8, "resonate", "clarity", 0.95),
])
```

## Install

```bash
pip install signal-notation
```

Or from source:
```bash
pip install git+https://github.com/theBullfish/signal-notation.git
```

